> I have created an experimental web service on the Jorne site. It uses
> Robin's PEG parser to create an XML parse tree based on Lojban text. It's
> not particularly tolerant of errors in the text - did I mention
> experimental? ;-) - and the output tree is not much to look at. Its purpose
> is not to be displayed directly, but to embed within Javascript calls for
> Lojban mashups.
>
> There is a web form that you can use to see how the service works.
> http://jorne.org/form.jsp
>
> The easiest way to build something on the XML result is to apply an XSL
> stylesheet that does some highlighting or text outlining. You are welcome to
> call the service from your own web site as long as it doesn't overwhelm the
> service with too many calls. I plan to make a stylesheet to pretty-print
> something better when I have some time.
>
> What will you build from it? Have at it, Lojban web developers!
